    <descript>
      <abstract>Station table and point layer for 33 Coastwide Reference Monitoring System (CRMS) hydrographic stations: 21 stations within 22 km of the center of Lake Maurepas and 4 key sites in each of the Pontchartrain, Barataria and Terrebonne basins. outputs/tables/crms_station_summary.csv (33 rows, 36 columns) gives, for each station, daily mean salinity statistics (mean, median, 10th and 90th percentiles, maximum, percent of days above 2 and 5 ppt), the seasonal cycle (saltiest and freshest month, seasonal range), seasonal Mann-Kendall salinity trends with seasonal Sen slopes for the full record and for 2013 to 2025, a water-level trend on GEOID12B from October 2013, and Benjamini-Hochberg FDR q values. data/crms_stations_selected.geojson (and the matching CSV) holds the station points in WGS 84 with group, basin, parish, vegetation type and record dates. Statistics come from the CPRA CRMS hourly 'adjusted' record reduced to daily means; trend tests use monthly means through December 2025.</abstract>
      <purpose>Portfolio and research product summarizing salinity intrusion and water-level change at CRMS stations for environmental science, coastal restoration and GIS use, and the source of the station placemarks and balloons in the Google Earth KMZ of the same repository.</purpose>
      <supplinf>Independent analysis of public data by Anamika Dristi, Ph.D.; it uses none of the author's LSU dissertation data. Code is MIT licensed. The lat and lon columns of crms_station_summary.csv are rounded to 0.01 degree (up to 641 m, median 451 m, from the full-precision positions); use the GeoJSON or data/crms_stations_selected.csv for station positions. Related tables: crms_monthly_climatology.csv, crms_group_trend_summary.csv and crms_hydro_station_inventory.csv in outputs/tables.</supplinf>
    </descript>
