      <procstep>
        <procdesc>Download (scripts/01_download_data.py): public keyless files fetched from CIMS, ScienceBase and USGS Water Services into the raw data folder (not committed).</procdesc>
        <srcused>CRMSHydro</srcused>
        <srcused>CIMSStations</srcused>
        <srcused>CIMSSites</srcused>
        <srcused>CWPPRABasins</srcused>
        <procdate>20261023</procdate>
      </procstep>
      <procstep>
        <procdesc>Daily means (scripts/02_build_crms_daily.py, 02_daily.awk): the 15 GB hourly CSV streamed from the zip and reduced to one row per station and day: mean adjusted salinity (ppt), adjusted water temperature, adjusted water elevation to datum (ft NAVD88), the number of hourly values and the geoid model. Only surface-water hydro stations (IDs ending -H01, -H02) kept; a daily mean needs at least 12 hourly values. Output: data/crms_selected_daily.csv.gz (selected stations).</procdesc>
        <srcused>CRMSHydro</srcused>
        <procdate>20261023</procdate>
      </procstep>
      <procstep>
        <procdesc>Station selection (scripts/03_select_stations.py): CRMS hydro station points (STATION_ID matching CRMSdddd-Hdd) projected to WGS 84 and joined to CWPPRA basins; vegetation type and parish joined from CRMS Sites. Lake Maurepas group = every station within 22 km of 30.255 N, 90.515 W with at least 8 years of record (21 stations). For each of the Pontchartrain, Barataria and Terrebonne basins, 4 key sites outside the Maurepas group picked evenly along latitude from stations with at least 3,650 days of daily salinity and data in 2025. Output: data/crms_stations_selected.csv; outputs/tables/crms_hydro_station_inventory.csv.</procdesc>
        <srcused>CIMSStations</srcused>
        <srcused>CIMSSites</srcused>
        <srcused>CWPPRABasins</srcused>
        <srcused>CRMSHydro</srcused>
        <procdate>20261023</procdate>
      </procstep>
      <procstep>
        <procdesc>Trends and summary (scripts/04_salinity_trends.py): daily values through 2025-12-31 averaged to monthly means (a month needs 15 valid days). Seasonal Mann-Kendall test with seasonal Sen slope (pymannkendall.seasonal_test, period 12) on the full record and on 2013 to 2025; water-level trend only on the longest run of days on one geoid model (GEOID12B from 2013-10-01 at every station). Benjamini-Hochberg false discovery rate q across the 33 stations. Daily salinity percentiles, exceedance shares and the seasonal cycle (mean of monthly means by calendar month) computed per station. Table written with 4 significant digits (pandas float_format %.4g). Output: outputs/tables/crms_station_summary.csv; outputs/tables/crms_monthly_climatology.csv; outputs/tables/crms_group_trend_summary.csv.</procdesc>
        <srcused>CRMSHydro</srcused>
        <procdate>20261023</procdate>
      </procstep>
      <procstep>
        <procdesc>GeoJSON export (scripts/06_maps.py): the selected station table converted to WGS 84 points from its lat and lon columns and written with the GDAL GeoJSON driver. Output: data/crms_stations_selected.geojson.</procdesc>
        <procdate>20261023</procdate>
      </procstep>
      <procstep>
        <procdesc>FGDC CSDGM metadata written from the README, the scripts and direct inspection of the CSV and GeoJSON with pandas and geopandas (columns, value ranges, CRS, extent, coordinate rounding).</procdesc>
        <procdate>20261024</procdate>
      </procstep>
